{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c68d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a086e5-19c2-72a1-a8e0-dd9212b1ae96"},"sequence":417,"recorded_at":1780531400000829,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"ee8c09f6-cc61-426f-a02a-8b2cf0e07f16"},"task_id":"ee8c09f6-cc61-426f-a02a-8b2cf0e07f16","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"ee8c09f6-cc61-426f-a02a-8b2cf0e07f16","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-16-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"v0\\\\.5\\\\.0\\\\|v0\\\\.6\\\\.0\\\\|specpin\\\\|specdoc\\\\|normative\\\" README.md | head -40; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"v0\\\\.6\\\\.0\\\" --include=\\\"*.go\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.json\\\" internal README.md LOGBOOK.md 2>/dev/null | grep -v specdoc/SPEC | head -20\",\n  \"description\": \"Find provenance docs and v0.6.0 mentions\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"9:v0.5.0 specification has been decomposed into an implementation board. The\\n10:Go contract foundation pins the immutable normative source and generates typed\\n19:[normative AX specification](https://github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec/blob/main/SPEC.md).\\n79:[`internal/specpin`](internal/specpin) embeds one implementation lock for\\n80:`agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0`. Its production `Current` and `Verify`\\n93:[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) embeds the byte-exact `SPEC.md` of that\\n97:normative; this copy is a verification input and amends nothing.\\n100:`specpin.DocumentSHA256`, so a substituted, edited, truncated, or unreadable\\n184:# exits non-zero: 0/31, 0/3, 0/5, 1/3 and 0/25 normative clauses discharged\\n376:its single normative clause is enumerated and discharged. Sections 3.2, 6.1,\\n422:against the digest-pinned document in `internal/specdoc`, quoting the exact\\n723:contract-version agreement derived from `internal/specpin` and\\n730:instrument, which the `specdoc` guard reserves to the existing repository\\n797:the pinned v0.5.0 source. The catalog contains the reviewed terminal, clone,\\n847:[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) document verbatim, beginning on the exact\\n866:come from, and `specdoc.SectionID` resolves every cited line to its nearest\\n1003:over the deepest normative closed shape (the 16-level submodule tree) and stays\\n1024:graph, and against the digest-pinned document in `internal/specdoc` — a quoted\\n1082:[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) does not yet gate them. Admitting an extra member, dropping one, reordering\\n1150:eight normative gates could be deleted from the core-record validators\\n1306:still be declared by v0.5.0. The detector is a pure function with its own\\n1421:Registry 1.0.0 bound to the pinned v0.5.0 Section 3.2 source. `ResolvePaths`\\n1626:| Exit-status registry | `ExitStatusMeaning` and `IsFailureExitStatus`, the closed Section 15.2 table, whose eighteen rows are measured from [`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) rather than restated in prose; success is never a failure class |\\n1679:constant still says it. Section 16.2 is explicit that v0.5.0 \\\"does not claim\\n1825:than described in prose. Section 14.2 coverage is 8 of its 9 normative clauses;\\n1936:normative examples verbatim, an envelope carrying a namespaced extension this\\n2199:`catalog.Current()` for v0.5.0 and `catalog.ForRelease()` for the exact pinned\\n2201:[`catalog.v0.5.0.json`](internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json); generation first\\n2202:verifies the exact [`specpin`](internal/specpin) lock, strictly rejects partial,\\n2211:| v0.5.0 | 60 | 99 | 46 | 112 | 109 |\\n2214:The source pin and catalog metadata cover every normative top-level section\\n2228:go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n2236:[`ownership.v0.5.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json)\\n2238:contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 98\\n2242:The generated v0.5.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\\n2261:the immutable v0.5.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\\n2279:[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc): the RFC 2119 clause lines the pinned\\n2288:| `full` | every normative clause of the section is enumerated and discharged | yes |\\n2299:normative exit-code registry, exited 0 with nothing in the tree implementing it,\\n2342:Fifty-three section bindings discharge 17 of the 428 normative clauses their\\n===\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3551,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 888,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
