{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7b9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a086e5-19c2-72a1-a8e0-dd9212b1ae96"},"sequence":567,"recorded_at":1780531400001129,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3"},"call_id":"call_01a086e8ad0e7a62a857f0696e6c1f34","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-24-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls ~/.agents/skills/go-testing-tools/references/ 2>/dev/null; head -60 ~/.agents/skills/go-testing-tools/references/negative-evidence.md 2>/dev/null; echo ===; tail -40 LOGBOOK.md; echo ===; sed -n '75,105p' README.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read evidence shapes, logbook, README provenance\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"cross-platform-setup-and-credentials.md\\nelm-architecture.md\\nmock-patterns.md\\ntesting-pyramid.md\\n===\\n- FIX: the waiter owns the bound now — `command.Wait()` runs in a goroutine under `select` on the call context, both drains collect through `collectDrains` under the same context, and closing the read ends fails blocked drains at once. A `Process.Kill` backstop covers a self-detached direct child, which the group-aimed `Cancel` misses. The round-6 EPIPE rule is untouched: with the wait reaped and stdout holding a frame, the frame still governs.\\n- ANOMALY: the first regression probe passed vacuously in 0.79s — python3 cold start under load can exceed the 400ms deadline kill, so no grandchild ever existed to hold the pipe. A hang test whose fixture loses a startup race proves nothing. Rebuilt on perl (millisecond start) with the kill seconds away; 3/3 red at the sleeper lifetime before the fix, green at the deadline after.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F2): the 13-vector corpus was literal-versus-literal — both implementations matched the same hand list, so a narrowed low-surrogate ceiling (SG1, 1023 admitted) and a narrowed uppercase hex range (SG5, 473 admitted) survived 6/6. Raw WTF-8 (`\\\\xed\\\\xa0\\\\x80`) arrived through an encoding the escape scanner never sees and became U+FFFD silently.\\n- FIX: `decodeStrictObject` refuses non-UTF-8 first (mirroring `canonicaljson.decodeStrict` order), and the corpus is replaced by a 239,630-vector derived sweep — full BMP x hex case, surrogate x 16 case mixes, high x boundary/non-low seconds, sampled positions plus all-surrogate member names, full BMP raw (WTF-8 form for surrogates), malformed patterns, astral samples — every verdict judged by the independent implementation. SG1 diverges on 19,482 vectors, SG5 on 4,411; gate removal reddens the identity row with err=nil and the sweep on 2,059.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F3): `checkResponseMembers` ran before the version gate, so only a v2-shaped 3.x envelope reached `incompatible_protocol`; the tree's own pinned 7.2 quote scopes that member rule to major 2. Fixed the ordering, not the doc: a `foreignMajor` peek (protocol identity plus readable foreign version, trusts nothing, refuses nothing) skips the v2 `ok`/member rules so the single existing mismatch site decides. No new refusal arm; floor untouched by F3.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/runner.go`, `protocol.go`, `surrogate*.go`, `identity.go` + comment corrections, `runner_test.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, refusal inventory (floor 164->166: one UTF-8 frame arm plus its status-body expansion, each witnessed).\\n- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32jeti: two green branches, one red combination — syscall.Mkfifo under GOOS=windows vet\\n- FINDING: the new CI step `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` failed on the merged tree with `terminalbackend_test.go:972:20: undefined: syscall.Mkfifo` — the only failure across all 16 packages. Invisible on both parents by construction: the story branch added the gate before the package existed (nothing to compile, exit 0), and trunk added the `syscall.Mkfifo` FIFO case without the gate (never compiled under Windows). Each branch was green on its own; only the combination is red. A per-branch gate that never meets the code it must check proves nothing about the merge.\\n- FIX: moved only the FIFO case out of `TestDigestFile` into `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` in new `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend_unix_test.go`, following the `internal/localstore/projection_unix_test.go` pattern. Correction worth recording: the `_unix` filename suffix alone constrains nothing (`unix` is a build tag, not a GOOS value, so the suffix form matches no `_GOOS` pattern) — the first attempt with suffix-only still failed windows vet, and the explicit `//go:build unix` line is what excludes Windows. The shared test file drops the `syscall` import and keeps a pointer comment; no other Go file touched.\\n- EVIDENCE: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 16/16 green with `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` observed PASS on linux (a moved test that stops executing is not a fix), `tracecheck` exit 0. TASK-260830-32jeti, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0: sessadapter closed-vocabulary census derived from the pinned document, vocab gates looped, acceptance cases registered\\n- FIX: `census_test.go` used `specdoc` without deriving from it (vet failure on the unused import). Added `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` (20 closed bodies: every Required list in document order plus the Members map as a set, with the success/failure envelopes derived by the spec's own first-four-fields rule, the manifest from its table's first-column spans, and the doctor result from the operation table) and `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec` (16 vocabularies pinned to their spec unions; operation/capability registries in order, value sets as sets).\\n- FINDINGS (all verified against the raw document, each would have been a silent wrong-source derivation): the request envelope sentence exists three times (7.5-style, 7.8, 7.9) and the capability-value sentence twice (Provider Probe 7.4 vs Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\\\\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).\\n- REFACTOR (production-first, same `var` + `validX` loop idiom the package already uses): `capabilityStatuses`/`validCapabilityStatus` (probe.go), `readPurposes`/`validReadPurpose` and `findingSeverities`/`validFindingSeverity` (context.go), `tupleArchitectures`/`validTupleArchitecture` (tuple.go); the four inline-literal checks now loop the tables. Roles, directions, candidate kinds, and platforms derive from the existing `Role`/`Direction`/`CandidateKind`/`scalar.Platform` consts with no production change (tuple platforms delegate to `scalar.ParsePlatform`).\\n- TEST: new `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status` — no behavioral test refused a fifth status, so a `return true` mutant of `validCapabilityStatus` survived the suite with the static census green. The mutant is now killed by the entry point (`DecodeProbe`).\\n- EVIDENCE (executed mutants, `/tmp/sessadapter-mutants.sh`, tree verified identical before/after): M1 `capabilityStatuses`+`bogus` killed by `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`; M2 `findingSeverities`+`fatal` killed by `TestDecodeFindingRules/bad_severity`; M3 `requestMembers`+`zzz` killed by `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec/request_envelope`; M4 `validCapabilityStatus`→`return true` (all searched-for tokens preserved) leaves the static census green and is killed by the behavioral suite (`TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status`); M5 unregistered vocabulary-shaped `var` killed by `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`. 8/8 as required, 0 survived.\\n- TRACEABILITY: 7 acceptance cases appended (`session-adapter-discovery/-manifest/-probe/-operations/-limits/-idempotency/-tuple-gates`, each bound to one production declaration and its named positive/refusal tests), digest re-pinned to `78d9bc9b...`, count pins 81->88, README ownership paragraph 81->88 plus a sessadapter disclosure paragraph that keeps the Section 7.8 clause-level binding `unevidenced` (no clause enumerated — no clause-level claim made).\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 5: B4/B5 closed as classes by derived denominators, N8 indirection refused\\n- FIX (B8): `bound_census_test.go` rosters all 97 production bound sites (six helpers by member, len guards by shape with values normalized out, DecodeFindings cap instantiations): 82 driven at entries both edges, 15 exempt (4 mechanism, 4 plumbing, 3 equivalent, 5 stated-bound 65536-count rows). `requireStringBounds`/`requireUint53Bounds` wrappers are mechanism rows; the 19 caller sites carry the rows.\\n- FIX (B7): `identity_census_test.go` rosters all 62 `X != Y` gates (mechanical classes excluded) plus a 5-row presence census with structural proof: 54 driven zero-on-exempted-side at exported entries (CheckProbe x6 both sides, seal 8x2, admission key x5 entry+binding sides, binding caller-side x4), 8 exempt (2 dispatch, 4 sentinel, 2 equivalent).\\n- FIX (N8): `constructorSitesInFile` reports any `axerror.New` selector outside call-fun position; synthetic proof covers package-level and function-local indirection (report) vs definition spelling and Decode (exempt).\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): `Bext-min` is genuinely equivalent (no 2-char key satisfies the reverse-DNS grammar); `Iops-candidate` is genuinely equivalent (both sides come from `requireDigestValue`); registry-element gates had no \\\"\\\" row (added `TestRegistryElementEmptyRefuses`); `Ituple-strategies` needed a struct-level [\\\"\\\"] row (added); `Ibind-tuple` first exempted the wrong side (context is never zero; corrected to the admitted side and killed). Len-guard census IDs briefly embedded values and caught a mutant statically — normalized to shape-only so values are pinned behaviorally, per the file's own documented design.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/battery.py`, 153 mutants applied by exact string, PRESENT-confirmed, restore-verified: 147 killed, 6 equivalent-confirmed (3 full-green, 3 behavioral-green with only the roster failing closed on the added clause), 0 survived, 0 not-applied. Additive probe file failed all three censuses naming the planted sites, then removed. Full table attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev5.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`bound_census_test.go`, `identity_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `zero_absent_test.go`); zero production changes, so no resurrections possible. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, `-cover` green (sessadapter 82.4%), `-race` green on the package, vet + gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 7: rev6 G-B closed — shape space enumerated per census, three shapes derived, residue bounded\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n===\\nplanning authority.\\n\\n## Normative Source Pin\\n\\n[`internal/specpin`](internal/specpin) embeds one implementation lock for\\n`agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0`. Its production `Current` and `Verify`\\nentry points fail closed on a partial read, unknown member, source substitution,\\ncontract or fixture drift, and any byte-level lock change. It also projects the\\nexact historical v0.4.3 registry without widening that immutable baseline.\\n\\nThis package is read-only and does not mutate durable state. Repeated reads are\\nidempotent and isolated from caller mutation. It deliberately adds no `ax`\\ncommand, `doctor` result, conformance-target declaration, or runtime capability\\nclaim; those surfaces remain unavailable until their owning implementation and\\nacceptance tasks land.\\n\\n## Pinned Specification Document\\n\\n[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) embeds the byte-exact `SPEC.md` of that\\nsame pinned release so repository fidelity gates can compare their artifacts\\nagainst the specification text instead of against the implementation those\\nartifacts are supposed to constrain. The upstream specification remains\\nnormative; this copy is a verification input and amends nothing.\\n\\n`Load` accepts the document only when its SHA-256 equals\\n`specpin.DocumentSHA256`, so a substituted, edited, truncated, or unreadable\\ndocument is refused rather than silently compared against — otherwise a swapped\\nspecification would confirm whatever it happened to contain. `QuoteLines`\\nresolves an excerpt to the 1-based `SPEC.md` lines it begins on, `SectionID`\\nresolves a line to the numbered clause that contains it, `TableRowAt` reports\\nwhat a Markdown table body row declares, and all three work under one\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 16150,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4038,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a086e5-19c2-72a1-a8e0-dd9212b1ae96"},"sequence":568,"recorded_at":1780531400001131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"98051fac-e595-413c-ab29-8cb5ece495f3"},"call_id":"call_01a086e8b0a074d0a2ad86caca8de6c9","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260908-18woqo/worktree/internal/traceability/traceability.go`.\n(219 line(s) above)\n220|\t}\n221|\n222|\tlockBytes, err := readRequired(repository, contractLockPath)\n223|\tif err != nil {\n224|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n225|\t}\n226|\tmanifest, err := specpin.Verify(lockBytes)\n227|\tif err != nil {\n228|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"verify normative source lock: %v\", err)\n229|\t}\n230|\n231|\tmetadataBytes, err := readRequired(repository, catalogMetadataPath)\n232|\tif err != nil {\n233|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n234|\t}\n235|\tgenerated, err := cataloggen.Generate(metadataBytes, lockBytes)\n236|\tif err != nil {\n237|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"verify reviewed catalog metadata: %v\", err)\n238|\t}\n239|\tcommittedGenerated, err := readRequired(repository, generatedCatalogPath)\n240|\tif err != nil {\n241|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n242|\t}\n243|\tif !bytes.Equal(generated, committedGenerated) {\n244|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"generated catalog is stale; run go generate ./internal/catalog\")\n245|\t}\n246|\n247|\tcurrentCatalog, err := catalog.ForRelease(catalog.ReleaseV050)\n248|\tif err != nil {\n249|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"load current catalog: %v\", err)\n250|\t}\n251|\tif err := verifyCatalogContracts(manifest.Contracts, currentCatalog.Contracts); err != nil {\n252|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n253|\t}\n254|\tcompatibilityCatalog, err := catalog.ForRelease(catalog.ReleaseV043)\n255|\tif err != nil {\n256|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"load compatibility catalog: %v\", err)\n257|\t}\n258|\n259|\tregistryBytes, err := readRequired(repository, ownershipRegistryPath)\n260|\tif err != nil {\n261|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n262|\t}\n263|\tregistry, err := decodeOwnershipRegistry(registryBytes)\n264|\tif err != nil {\n265|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n266|\t}\n267|\tbindings, err := resolveAssignedSections(manifest.Source.NormativeScope, assignedSections)\n268|\tif err != nil {\n269|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n270|\t}\n271|\tdocument, err := specdoc.Load()\n272|\tif err != nil {\n273|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"load pinned specification document: %v\", err)\n274|\t}\n275|\tif manifest.Source.Document.SHA256 != specpin.DocumentSHA256 {\n276|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\n277|\t\t\t\"verified normative lock document digest %s differs from the pinned clause source %s\",\n278|\t\t\tmanifest.Source.Document.SHA256, specpin.DocumentSHA256)\n279|\t}\n280|\treturn verifyOwnership(repository, document, registry, manifest, currentCatalog, compatibilityCatalog, bindings)\n281|}\n282|\n283|func readRequired(repository fs.FS, filename string) ([]byte, error) {\n284|\tvalue, err := fs.ReadFile(repository, filename)\n285|\tif err != nil {\n286|\t\treturn nil, fail(\"read required evidence %q: %v\", filename, err)\n287|\t}\n288|\treturn value, nil\n289|}\n290|\n291|func decodeOwnershipRegistry(candidate []byte) (ownershipRegistry, error) {\n292|\tvar decoded ownershipRegistry\n293|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(candidate))\n294|\tdecoder.DisallowUnknownFields()\n295|\tif err := decoder.Decode(&decoded); err != nil {\n296|\t\treturn ownershipRegistry{}, fail(\"decode ownership registry: %v\", err)\n297|\t}\n298|\tvar trailing any\n299|\tif err := decoder.Decode(&trailing); !errors.Is(err, io.EOF) {\n300|\t\tif err == nil {\n301|\t\t\treturn ownershipRegistry{}, fail(\"decode ownership registry: multiple JSON values\")\n302|\t\t}\n303|\t\treturn ownershipRegistry{}, fail(\"decode ownership registry trailing data: %v\", err)\n304|\t}\n305|\treturn decoded, nil\n306|}\n307|\n308|func verifyOwnership(\n309|\trepository fs.FS,\n310|\tdocument *specdoc.Document,\n311|\tregistry ownershipRegistry,\n312|\tmanifest specpin.Manifest,\n313|\tcurrentCatalog catalog.Catalog,\n314|\tcompatibilityCatalog catalog.Catalog,\n315|\tassignedBindings []assignedSectionBinding,\n316|) (Report, error) {\n317|\tif registry.Format != ownershipFormat || registry.FormatVersion != ownershipFormatVersion {\n318|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"unsupported ownership registry format %q version %d\", registry.Format, registry.FormatVersion)\n319|\t}\n320|\tsource := registry.Source\n321|\tif source.Repository != manifest.Source.Repository ||\n322|\t\tsource.Release != manifest.Source.Release ||\n323|\t\tsource.Commit != manifest.Source.Commit ||\n324|\t\tsource.DocumentPath != manifest.Source.Document.Path ||\n325|\t\tsource.DocumentSHA256 != manifest.Source.Document.SHA256 {\n326|\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"ownership registry source differs from verified normative lock\")\n327|\t}\n328|\n329|\texpected := map[ownershipKind]map[string]struct{}{\n330|\t\townershipContract:         expectedContracts(manifest.Contracts),\n331|\t\townershipNormativeSection: expectedNormativeSections(manifest, currentCatalog),\n332|\t\townershipSectionBinding:   expectedSectionBindingInventory(),\n333|\t\townershipFixture:          expectedFixtures(manifest, currentCatalog),\n334|\t}\n335|\trequiredSectionBindings, err := expectedCatalogSectionBindings(currentCatalog)\n336|\tif err != nil {\n337|\t\treturn Report{}, err\n338|\t}\n339|\trequired := map[ownershipKind]map[string]struct{}{\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
